    "markdown": "---\ntitle: overlay_weights\n---\n\n\n\n```python\noverlay_weights(source, target, id_col='geo_id')\n```\n\nArea of every source-target intersection, in an equal-area projection.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name   | Type   | Description                                              | Default    |\n|--------|--------|----------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| source |        | Scale ids, or GeoDataFrames with ``id_col`` and polygons | _required_ |\n| target |        | Scale ids, or GeoDataFrames with ``id_col`` and polygons | _required_ |\n| id_col | str    | The id column of GeoDataFrame inputs                     | `'geo_id'` |\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                  |\n|--------|------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | pandas.DataFrame | Columns ``geo_id_from``, ``geo_id_to``, ``area_km2``, ``share_of_from`` (the part of the source unit inside the target) and ``share_of_to``. |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\nw = geo.overlay_weights(\"municipality\", \"department\")\npx.histogram(w, x=\"share_of_from\", log_y=True,\n             title=\"Share of each municipality inside each department\")\n```\n\n\n::: {#3143db23 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font